This package contains backhand (https://github.com/wcampbell0x2a/backhand),
version 0.25.3, commit eccf81b6f599cb90245d7c9694e95ee6023cad06,
licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, by wcampbell0x2a and contributors.

Turen added a bounded WebAssembly wrapper (squashfs_list / squashfs_extract)
and applies one maintained patch (patches/0001-wasm-osstr.patch) that adds a
non-unix/non-Windows OsStr byte fallback so the crate compiles for
wasm32-unknown-unknown.

backhand is built with a reduced pure-Rust feature set: gzip (flate2 +
zlib-rs), lz4 (lz4_flex), and v3 image support. The following upstream
features are intentionally disabled:

  - lzo        — the selected decompressor is GPL-licensed.
  - v3_lzma /  — pull in lzma-adaptive-sys, C++ code containing GPL-2.0
    v4_lzma      material; not compatible with this artifact's license
                 closure. Affected vendor kinds (qshs, shsq, lzma v4) report
                 unsupported_kind / unsupported_compression.
  - xz         — pulls in liblzma-sys (native C build).
  - zstd       — pulls in zstd-sys (native C build).
  - parallel   — rayon threading; not applicable to single-threaded WASM.

Images using those compressors are detected and report explicit
unsupported_compression errors rather than failing silently.

